Today I focused on transforming my pivot table analysis into PivotCharts to create more meaningful visual insights for my HR Gender Diversity & Equality dashboard.

After preparing the data and calculating key HR metrics, I built visualizations that help highlight salary distribution and compensation patterns across different departments.

Visualizations Created
	•	Annual Salary by Department
Chart Type: Bar Chart
Purpose: To analyze how salary expenses are distributed across departments.
	•	Compensation by Department
Chart Type: Bar Chart
Purpose: To compare the total compensation allocated to each department.

Dashboard Features
	•	Implemented interactive slicers for:
	•	Gender
	•	Branch
	•	Department

These slicers allow users to dynamically filter the dashboard and explore the workforce data from different perspectives.

Key Takeaway

Using PivotCharts helped transform raw HR data into clear visual insights, making it easier to analyze departmental salary structures and compensation trends.
